$DIR/test.p:14:19: impossible type assertion: x.(*S)
	*S does not implement I (method Id has type parameters, so it cannot implement an interface method)
		have Id[U any]() int
		want Id() int
    The type in the assertion does not have every method of the interface, so no
    value of the interface can hold it, and the assertion would always fail.
    (see "Type assertions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.13)
    (run "pluto explain E0095" for a longer explanation)
